                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6b2775f-a1c0-3e6a-8348-6328edd87b45",
                        "entry_id": "9fe2f812-9d4a-3a6b-a5d5-7abb17fc5e13",
                        "glosses": [
                            "什錦蔬菜/水果"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "94e6ef33-72cb-47e5-9793-4873aa11dea7",
                                "sense_id": "d6b2775f-a1c0-3e6a-8348-6328edd87b45",
                                "text": "This one is a mixture of textures and tastes and all kinds of vegetables—that's why it is called a macédoine. It's an odd route from Alexander the Great to your table, but Alexander, a Macedonian, had an empire consisting of many disparate states.",
                                "translation": "这道菜混合了各种口感和味道，还有不同的蔬菜品种——这就是为什么它被称为“什锦蔬菜”（macédoine）。这就像是亚历山大大帝走了一条奇怪的路线，一直走到你的餐桌上。亚历山大是马其顿人，他的帝国由许多迥异的国家组成。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6b9a81b-b928-49c5-abf9-aa03a3ae356c",
                                "sense_id": "d6b2775f-a1c0-3e6a-8348-6328edd87b45",
                                "text": "We chilled it in a wonderful old French copper mold that we borrowed, naturally，源自Lucullus, and surrounded it with a macédoine of fruit.",
                                "translation": "我们把它放在一个奇妙的法国老铜制模具里冷藏，这个铜模自然是从卢库鲁斯那里借来的，并在它周围放上什锦水果。"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "702a0330-4512-33e3-ab2e-42b65cbdaafe",
                        "entry_id": "9fe2f812-9d4a-3a6b-a5d5-7abb17fc5e13",
                        "glosses": [
                            "混搭，雜燴"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c92c589-bab9-4fb3-bc6d-6287481d8a14",
                                "sense_id": "702a0330-4512-33e3-ab2e-42b65cbdaafe",
                                "text": "Actually, this ethnic situation—a “macédoine” of peoples—was complicated even more from the 1860s on when some of the Slavs in Macedonia who had always called themselves Bulgarians (and were considered so by most foreign experts) began developing a Macedonian national consciousness.",
                                "translation": "实际上，从19世纪60年代开始，这种各民族“大杂烩”的状况变得更加复杂，当时一些一直自称是保加利亚人（而且也被大多数外国专家认为是保加利亚人）的马其顿斯拉夫人，开始形成马其顿的民族意识。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
